STEP 1. Install Java JDK 1.8
Download Java JDK 1.8 from Oracle:
Java SE JDK 8 Downloads

Install it in C:\Java.

Verify installation:
javac -version

STEP 2. Download Hadoop
Get Hadoop 3.3.0 from Apache:
Hadoop 3.3.0 (apache.org in Bing)

Extract to:
C:\Hadoop-3.3.0

STEP 3. Set Environment Variables
Add JAVA_HOME → C:\Java\jdk1.8.0_361

Add HADOOP_HOME → C:\Hadoop-3.3.0

Update PATH to include bin directories of both Java and Hadoop.

STEP 4. Configure Hadoop XML Files
<configuration>
  <property>
    <name>fs.defaultFS</name>
    <value>hdfs://localhost:9000</value>
  </property>
</configuration>
mapred-site.xml
(rename mapred-site.xml.template → mapred-site.xml)

xml
<configuration>
  <property>
    <name>mapreduce.framework.name</name>
    <value>yarn</value>
  </property>
</configuration>
hdfs-site.xml
xml
<configuration>
  <property>
    <name>dfs.replication</name>
    <value>1</value>
  </property>
  <property>
    <name>dfs.namenode.name.dir</name>
    <value>/hadoop-3.3.0/data/namenode</value>
  </property>
  <property>
    <name>dfs.datanode.data.dir</name>
    <value>/hadoop-3.3.0/data/datanode</value>
  </property>
</configuration>
yarn-site.xml
xml
<configuration>
  <property>
    <name>yarn.nodemanager.aux-services</name>
    <value>mapreduce_shuffle</value>
  </property>
  <property>
    <name>yarn.nodemanager.auxservices.mapreduce.shuffle.class</name>
    <value>org.apache.hadoop.mapred.ShuffleHandler</value>
  </property>
  <property>
    <name>yarn.resourcemanager.address</name>
    <value>127.0.0.1:8032</value>
  </property>
  <property>
    <name>yarn.resourcemanager.scheduler.address</name>
    <value>127.0.0.1:8030</value>
  </property>
  <property>
    <name>yarn.resourcemanager.resource-tracker.address</name>
    <value>127.0.0.1:8031</value>
  </property>
</configuration>
5. Set Java Home in Hadoop
Edit hadoop-env.cmd:


set JAVA_HOME="C:\Java\jdk1.8.0_361"

STEP 6. Install Redistributable Package
Download and run VC_redist.x64.exe (Visual C runtime for 64‑bit apps).

STEP 7. Add Windows-Compatible Bin Folder
Download from GitHub:
Winutils for Hadoop (github.com in Bing)

Replace the existing bin folder in C:\Hadoop-3.3.0.

STEP 8. Format the NameNode
bash
hdfs namenode -format
STEP 9. Start Hadoop Services
bash
cd C:\Hadoop-3.3.0\sbin
start-all.cmd
Or run individually:

start-dfs.cmd
start-yarn.cmd

STEP 10. Verify Installation
jps
NameNode
DataNode
ResourceManager
NodeManager

Open browser:
http://localhost:9870 → Explore HDFS.
